  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Enhancing Mobility Monitoring and Border Coordination to Inform Preparedness Plans in Zimbabwe</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IOM Zimbabwe maintains the largest infrastructure for collecting data on flows of people across Southern Africa. IOM, through its Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) tools, has actively been working for the last two years with national and local authorities in order to gain a better understanding of population movements in the country and in the Region. This project seeks to strengthen IOM&apos;s support protection services, post-arrival assistance to migrants and flow monitoring activities at points of entry, border communities, and congregation points through data collection, analysis, and statistics on migration trends to provide a more comprehensive picture of mobility dynamics. Information collected will serve as a stronger evidence base for humanitarian response, development planning and operations with a regional analysis.</narrative>
  </description>
